{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions","id":273317,"title":"Some Demon: The Fallen questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-05T16:38:16-07:00","id":273317,"title":"Some Demon: The Fallen questions","content":"I'm currently in a Mage campaign with one Changeling also in it. I've been wanting to try playing a Demon, so I convinced my storyteller to let me do so using the excuse that my mage will leave the group for an extended period of time to study and learn(basically spend a bunch of stored experience). Before I start playing, there are some questions I have regarding Demons.<br /> <br /> 1. Lore Of Paths, specifically the second level power Lay Path. What are the limitations on this power? Could I use it to walk into a locked bank vault, bypassing the door? Is it creating space, warping space, or something else entirely? What do people outside of the path see when you walk it? Could I lay a path and walk on the ceiling for a short distance?<br /> <br /> 2. The Umbra. Do Demons even know about it? Can they travel to the near umbras with any of their abilities, or are they limited to the shadowlands? Where does the abilities in Lore Of The Realms take you, and what kind of things can Lore Of The Spirit let you talk to?<br /> <br /> 3. Using multiple Lores at once. Can you combine the effects of multiple Lores into a single effect, or are they one-at-a-time only? Or is that the point of rituals, combining two Lores for a single effect?<br /> <br /> I might think of more things as I encounter them, like do low torment Demons(Torment of 3) show up as Wyrm creatures to werewolves?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> 4. How does Extinguish Life affect other supernaturals? Would it kill a vampire? Werewolf? Changeling? Mage? H.I.T. Mark?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3716,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","user":"Mrtwist","date":". 10-05-2014, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T17:26:54-07:00","id":273337,"title":"","content":"Cant remember the ones about specific effects or lores but lemme see what i can do (puts on his reading glasses) <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bYu5PWld89g\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bYu5PWld89g</a><br /> The answers im going to give are not related to the Cannon in any form, but mainly to RP experiences and to discussions i had with other ST about the WoD<br /> <br /> 1._ I cant remember the exact effect, i would need to look through my book and its too far away xD + im busy xD.<br /> <br /> but lemme see what i can recal...<br /> What are the limitations on this power? <br /> Distance = Your Faith score on Meters.<br /> <br /> Could I use it to walk into a locked bank vault, bypassing the door?<br /> You could, but you would have to make a path with the open safe door. or you would end up crashing against the door. i mainly use it through open spaces or places with entrances and exists. Also, you could do that but...i dont recomend it, mainly because the Demonic Court (if youre using them) woudnt like to be spotted or be found. Also, i dont think the Syndicate would like that (Technocratic Union), for more information watch or read Jumper.<br /> <br /> Is it creating space, warping space, or something else entirely?<br /> Its not creating space, its altering distance. making the distance from point A to B shorter or longer. Ever seen on the movies or cartoons how suddenly the characters see a path and starts pulling and becoming eternal? pretty much that. or how in cartoons they suddenly jump from one scene to another? pretty much that.<br /> <br /> What do people outside of the path see when you walk it? <br /> Depends on your Torment Level, The higher it is, its something that could make someone go Mad. <a href=\"http://www.mcescher.com/Gallery/back-bmp/LW375.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.mcescher.com/Gallery/back-bmp/LW375.jpg</a><br /> Depends on how you want to play it, to be an Alien Geomethry and break laws of logic, or something incredibly more sutil.<br /> <br /> Could I lay a path and walk on the ceiling for a short distance?<br /> To literally walk through walls in a vertical way? theres Lore of Fundaments for that.<br /> To actually be able to open a door and appear on the roof top? yeah sure why not :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2._ Mainly the Halaku/Slayers-Not the Metal Band- are aware of this place, they usually travel to the Shadowloands. Can they go to other realms? (acording to me? Yes...but its not safe). Lore of Realms may take you to any place youre aware and studied before, its not like throwing a D20 to Pick a place..rather a place that has an intimate connection to the fallen one.<br /> Any spirit really, be a Wraith, or what ever comes fromthe Umbra on Mage or Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3._ Rituals really. On my game i work the Lores as the Spheres from mage (Its incredibly over powerful, but each time you use them, its easier for your name to be revealed and to pinpoint your location)<br /> <br /> Torment Torment Torment....Ok....This got two versions, long story short or short story long.<br /> LSS:<br /> Demons are Not just any wyrm creature..they are the closest thing to PARTS OF THE WYRM which can only get more horrible and more disturbing. Fomoris aware of Demons are actually afraid of them because of their Alien/Eldritch Horror Nature.<br /> How do Demons explains their taint to other creatures? they dont. When you play a demon you must and should forget about the Triad and rather take a more lovecraftian approach to the subject at hand. To quote one of my favorite movies when it comes to the Demon Nature and their &quot;Taint.&quot; in relation to the Wyrm. <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0000152/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\">John Klein</a>: I think we can assume that these entities are more advanced than us. Why don't they just come right out and tell us what's on their minds?<br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0000869/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\">Alexander Leek</a>: You're more advanced than a cockroach, have you ever tried explaining yourself to one of them?<br /> -The Mothman Prophecies.<br /> <br /> Some of the Werewolf players i encounter have this Horrifying idea that demons are something even more evil and primal than the Wyrm, something even ancient than the Wyrm itself which they cant classify (Which in term, its even more scary).<br /> <br /> 4._ Vampires, Mages, Hunters, Werewolves = Indiana Jones: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LRSjKfvm368\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LRSjKfvm368</a> , Im not entirely familiar with the Changeling Mythos but if you did this to the human...well, look at Indiana Jones, if you do this to the changeling. i suppose it would have to roll in order not to Age or he would grow too old and die.<br /> <br /> Hitmarks, Do elaborate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 10-05-2014, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T19:17:47-07:00","id":273423,"title":"","content":"Hey, I run a W:tA game and I am going to have Demons show up with Sense Wyrm no mater what their torment or faith score is. But I am also having them show up with Sense Weaver and Sense Wyld. the reason being they are from before the Tirat came into being, they are from the beginning of everything and so show up as all three. That's just my take on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T19:33:24-07:00","id":273432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273423#post273423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I run a W:tA game and I am going to have Demons show up with Sense Wyrm no mater what their torment or faith score is. But I am also having them show up with Sense Weaver and Sense Wyld. the reason being they are from before the Tirat came into being, they are from the beginning of everything and so show up as all three. That's just my take on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgot that little detail. Demons are Incredibly Alien when they come to terms to the Triat, some might be closer to some elements, and others may encompass all three of them. Thats why they are so scary to werewolves, because Demons are the equivelant of Alien Beings, even more Alien than the Wyrm Itself (and according to my games, the Wyrm is baffled and Mystified by this beings.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T23:04:22-07:00","id":273496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273432#post273432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forgot that little detail. Demons are Incredibly Alien when they come to terms to the Triat, some might be closer to some elements, and others may encompass all three of them. Thats why they are so scary to werewolves, because Demons are the equivelant of Alien Beings, even more Alien than the Wyrm Itself (and according to my games, the Wyrm is baffled and Mystified by this beings.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you do Werewolf's setting a disservice, because when the Wyrm feels strong emotions, to the extent that it can be said to, it spawns spiritual beings of vast power that could casually crush Earthbound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T23:22:06-07:00","id":273500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273496#post273496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then you do Werewolf's setting a disservice, because when the Wyrm feels strong emotions, to the extent that it can be said to, it spawns spiritual beings of vast power that could casually crush Earthbound.</div> </div> </div> </div>i dont run werewolf the apocalypse, im pretty sure theres hundreds of things on that game that could easly take down an Earthbound. I repeat, this is according to my world, im not taking any other information outside of what i ran and outside the knowledge i gained on some of the lores. I dont run werewolf, im familiar with some of the concepts on its mythology and such.<br /> <br /> To Me, demons are more ancient than the Triad, So much so that they lie outside the concepts of the triad. because they are the triad and yet they are not, they are an anomality you cant define. Yes, the wyrm can spawn spiritual beings of so much power that they could crush an Earthbound...i wont deny that...what i might deny is Which Earthbound.<br /> <br /> Take a Lesser Earthbound, one is dangerous enough to level a whole city like Los Angeles or NY... Why? because their power come from Faith, something intrincically human. the most powerful energy and source there can be. Gnosis its basically Mana, the spiritual element within everything, right?<br /> <br /> Well, faith its a bit more intrincated since its Something that Every being, no matter what condition has, something that everyone can develop (im not talking about True Faith) or anything like that, something powerful enough that could easly kill GOD (the Christian one) or turn off the Sun. Something so powerful that humans can use it with out noticing it. What happends when you feed a creature that pretty much created a Concept with this?.<br /> The Wyrm is a concept. we cant deny that<br /> but what is more powerful, the creation? or the Creator? the Maker or the Creation?.<br /> <br /> For what i gathered, the Apocalypse takes place in the Umbra rather than the physical world, the final battle its on another plane of existance against The Wyrm.<br /> <br /> While the Earth..well...you got yourself 5 creatures with cults and sects constantly feeding them, old and ancient, patient and yet powerful enough to break any law of physics with out having to pay any sort of price. the Wyrm its a Cosmical Horror, Earthbounds CREATED the Cosmic Horrors. they are the ones that allowed humans to be horrible. So in that context, i belive earthbounds are as powerful and as destructive or even more than the Wyrm.<br /> Make the 5 Big Ones (Belial, Dagon, Asmodeus, Azrael and Abbadon) do an alliance against the triad and things would end up pretty fucked up for everyone and everything<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S : This one <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kupala\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kupala</a> Is a lesser one, he is known as The Talon of The Wyrm. And yes, he is a lesser earthbound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T06:02:35-07:00","id":273690,"title":"","content":"WELL, Kupala is a earthbound only in Demon the fallen lore <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> But anyway, I gonna ask a question of my own, as im going to start runing Demon chronicle soon (TM)<br /> <br /> -The pacts: The system for the pacts I rather like, but I am confused, as it dosent seem to allow to use one's lore to make the &quot;Gift&quot;. As far as I understood it from the book, you need to spend one point of mortals potential faith to be crafted into a gift, so far so good, BUT, then it proceeds to give a very static list of Thrall Empowerments, and saying that the point of faith should be used on empowering your thrall from the list. Am I getting something wrong here? I love the idea of the gift and pact, but the whole &quot;Your gift can only be something that empowers the thrall bit&quot; seems incredibly limiting and counter-intuitive. Couldnt you, lets say, spend thralls point of faith, to create a gift using your lores? Or the gift couldnt be just healing someone, or just saving someone close to the thrall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1663-animalgod","name":"AnimalGod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1663_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T07:00:45-07:00","id":273779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273337#post273337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could I use it to walk into a locked bank vault, bypassing the door?<br /> You could, but you would have to make a path with the open safe door. or you would end up crashing against the door. i mainly use it through open spaces or places with entrances and exists. Also, you could do that but...i dont recomend it, mainly because the Demonic Court (if youre using them) woudnt like to be spotted or be found. Also, i dont think the Syndicate would like that (Technocratic Union), for more information watch or read Jumper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so you're saying Lay Path requires the path to be physically possible? So I can't use it to enter locked rooms or cross a wide river without getting wet? Any physical obstacles I would normally encounter would still be encountered on the path created? The first level of this Lore lets you find an existing path, and an example given was find a safe path through a raging house fire. The second level, which I'm talking about, lets you lay paths instead of just finding them. Using the example of the house fire, does this mean if a safe path can't be found through the house fire with the first level power then it also can't be created with the second level because the fire is still an existing obstacle that can't be avoided? <br /> <br /> The problem with this interpretaton is that the high torment version of the power specifically mentions paths under a lake or through a mountain, suggesting you're bypassing obstacles in-between two points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273337#post273337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it creating space, warping space, or something else entirely?<br /> Its not creating space, its altering distance. making the distance from point A to B shorter or longer. Ever seen on the movies or cartoons how suddenly the characters see a path and starts pulling and becoming eternal? pretty much that. or how in cartoons they suddenly jump from one scene to another? pretty much that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really get the first example there, but the second example seems to suggest jumping between two points without crossing the intervening distance. Combined with what I mentioned before, it's almost like the Demon is creating a personalized wormhole between two points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273337#post273337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do people outside of the path see when you walk it?<br /> Depends on your Torment Level, The higher it is, its something that could make someone go Mad. <a href=\"http://www.mcescher.com/Gallery/back-bmp/LW375.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.mcescher.com/Gallery/back-bmp/LW375.jpg</a><br /> Depends on how you want to play it, to be an Alien Geomethry and break laws of logic, or something incredibly more sutil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant what do other people see, not those on the path. If I lay a path from Point A to Point B and begin to walk it, what does the average Joe standing twenty feet away see me do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273337#post273337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could I lay a path and walk on the ceiling for a short distance?<br /> To literally walk through walls in a vertical way? theres Lore of Fundaments for that.<br /> To actually be able to open a door and appear on the roof top? yeah sure why not :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking of Lay Path as a path that exists in visible space, but it seems the more I write this that it's actually a wormhole-like creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273337#post273337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4._ Vampires, Mages, Hunters, Werewolves = Indiana Jones: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LRSjKfvm368\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LRSjKfvm368</a> , Im not entirely familiar with the Changeling Mythos but if you did this to the human...well, look at Indiana Jones, if you do this to the changeling. i suppose it would have to roll in order not to Age or he would grow too old and die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using youtube links isn't really helpful. Are you saying that other supernaturals are resistant to it's Insta-Kill effect in exactly the same way as Demons? The power itself states that it separates the soul from the body, killing them instantly. Vampires might be immune because they're not alive, but could it instantly kill an angry werewolf if I get more successes than it has Stamina?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273337#post273337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hitmarks, Do elaborate.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Hyper_Intelligence_Technologies\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Hype...e_Technologies</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T07:39:40-07:00","id":273812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273500#post273500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i dont run werewolf the apocalypse, im pretty sure theres hundreds of things on that game that could easly take down an Earthbound. I repeat, this is according to my world, im not taking any other information outside of what i ran and outside the knowledge i gained on some of the lores. I dont run werewolf, im familiar with some of the concepts on its mythology and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not incredibly familiar, it would seem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To Me, demons are more ancient than the Triad, So much so that they lie outside the concepts of the triad. because they are the triad and yet they are not, they are an anomality you cant define. Yes, the wyrm can spawn spiritual beings of so much power that they could crush an Earthbound...i wont deny that...what i might deny is Which Earthbound.<br /> <br /> Take a Lesser Earthbound, one is dangerous enough to level a whole city like Los Angeles or NY... Why? because their power come from Faith, something intrincically human. the most powerful energy and source there can be. Gnosis its basically Mana, the spiritual element within everything, right? </div> </div> </div>I'll have to make more reminders to avoid these discussions in the future, because I keep forgetting that Demon is as antithetical to Werewolf as Mage. Humans are on no special pedestal in Werewolf, and they have no special spiritual powers, from Faith or from Gnosis. Right away, there's some serious, irreconcilable cosmological conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, faith its a bit more intrincated since its Something that Every being, no matter what condition has, something that everyone can develop (im not talking about True Faith) or anything like that, something powerful enough that could easly kill GOD (the Christian one) or turn off the Sun. Something so powerful that humans can use it with out noticing it. What happends when you feed a creature that pretty much created a Concept with this?.<br /> The Wyrm is a concept. we cant deny that<br /> but what is more powerful, the creation? or the Creator? the Maker or the Creation?. </div> </div> </div>There's a great deal of disagreement over what the maker actually is or was, or if there was one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For what i gathered, the Apocalypse takes place in the Umbra rather than the physical world, the final battle its on another plane of existance against The Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>That's one scenario in a dated, end-of-the-line scenario book. Another one involves an asteroid slamming into Earth (courtesy of Rorg, the Asteroid Belt Incarna) and bringing on an era of desperate and very physical conflict, and another is that the Weaver pulls in from behind to snatch a surprise victory requiring all of the Garou and Fera to march into Malfeas and use all of their spiritual power to free the Wyrm and essentially restart the entire cosmos. And one involving another tribe falling, but that one isn't really well-favored.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the Earth..well...you got yourself 5 creatures with cults and sects constantly feeding them, old and ancient, patient and yet powerful enough to break any law of physics with out having to pay any sort of price. the Wyrm its a Cosmical Horror, Earthbounds CREATED the Cosmic Horrors. they are the ones that allowed humans to be horrible. So in that context, i belive earthbounds are as powerful and as destructive or even more than the Wyrm.<br /> Make the 5 Big Ones (Belial, Dagon, Asmodeus, Azrael and Abbadon) do an alliance against the triad and things would end up pretty fucked up for everyone and everything </div> </div> </div>Demons are all wigged out from imprisonment in the Abyss, which may or may not be the same Abysses in other games. They talk an awful lot about participating in Creation, but that's never narratively given as a certainty. If you want it to be, sure, but I think that you're better off not using anything from Werewolf at all if you want a pure Demon game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> P.S : This one <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kupala\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kupala</a> Is a lesser one, he is known as The Talon of The Wyrm. And yes, he is a lesser earthbound. </div> </div> </div>Kupala is not a Talon of the Wyrm. Talons of the Wyrm include Koschei, Narlthus, Thrassus, and one or two others who are canonically not Kupala and there for the ST to define on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T09:42:45-07:00","id":273936,"title":"","content":"I think we need a higher authority in this debate xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T11:49:33-07:00","id":274072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273936#post273936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we need a higher authority in this debate xD</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah! A Demon fan would say that. (^VVVVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T11:55:44-07:00","id":274077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273936#post273936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we need a higher authority in this debate xD</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is a question of authority- outwardly, both demons and the Wyrm evoke Lovecraftian imagery, but they are critical irreconcilable differences in theme and scope. The struggle of DtF is not the same as the war the Garou are waging in WtA. The pseudo-Judeo-Christian Fall background of Demon does not really mesh with the feral animism of Werewolf's Triat, at all. The Wyrm, the Wyld and the Weaver are not so much beings as they are spiritual underpinnings of the universe. They are vast entities so potent they create gods on accident. Kind of hard to get that to jive with Lucifer and the Fallen... and Saur Ops Specialist is right about humanity. In Werewolf, humans are a necessary nuisance at best, and the rapists murderers of the planet at worst. Demon is about human (and Fallen) worth and potential.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the easiest way to reconcile the two in a given game is just make one side largely correct, cosmologically speaking, and stick with it. All the other werewolves, vampires and will-workers are, by extension, deluded or mad.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T12:21:43-07:00","id":274091,"title":"","content":"And if you do go that route, you're going to need to clip some things back in order to fit the different pieces into your games. Vampire is a game that has nothing to do with spirits, so the Lupines encountered in the Antagonists section might have bizarre cults, but little to nothing about spirits is involved to keep the game in the boundaries that the V:TM core sets. Demon would likely follow the same path, especially since it never mentions spirits that aren't ghosts, I think.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, Fallen are extremely difficult to differentiate from powerful banes. In Werewolf, they would be quasi-spiritual beings that have a heavy tang of corruption about them but don't hang around the body after the Garou or Fera exorcise it, possibly in a very physical manner. Any more substantive explanation of their existence is likely to involve the old, maddened spirits of earlier geological periods that don't have much to do, like the Niobrara-spirit introduced in the W20 Book of the Wyrm. Mokole are likely to be much more familiar with them than others, other than a really old Rokea that met them but didn't care overly much about it, because you see weirder shit in a long war against the Chulorviah and merrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T20:18:00-07:00","id":274431,"title":"","content":"Another question. Some of the Demon Lores can improve stats, specifically referring to Lore Of The Flesh. Can these abilities be used to improve other supernatural creatures, such as werewolves and vampires, and even more importantly can they be used to improve the Fallen themselves? Could someone use the level three ability of Lore Of The Flesh to boost their own physical stats for combat purposes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T21:18:45-07:00","id":274468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrtwist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=273779#post273779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, so you're saying Lay Path requires the path to be physically possible? So I can't use it to enter locked rooms or cross a wide river without getting wet? Any physical obstacles I would normally encounter would still be encountered on the path created? The first level of this Lore lets you find an existing path, and an example given was find a safe path through a raging house fire. The second level, which I'm talking about, lets you lay paths instead of just finding them. Using the example of the house fire, does this mean if a safe path can't be found through the house fire with the first level power then it also can't be created with the second level because the fire is still an existing obstacle that can't be avoided?<br /> <br /> The problem with this interpretaton is that the high torment version of the power specifically mentions paths under a lake or through a mountain, suggesting you're bypassing obstacles in-between two points.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't really get the first example there, but the second example seems to suggest jumping between two points without crossing the intervening distance. Combined with what I mentioned before, it's almost like the Demon is creating a personalized wormhole between two points.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I meant what do other people see, not those on the path. If I lay a path from Point A to Point B and begin to walk it, what does the average Joe standing twenty feet away see me do?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm thinking of Lay Path as a path that exists in visible space, but it seems the more I write this that it's actually a wormhole-like creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Using youtube links isn't really helpful. Are you saying that other supernaturals are resistant to it's Insta-Kill effect in exactly the same way as Demons? The power itself states that it separates the soul from the body, killing them instantly. Vampires might be immune because they're not alive, but could it instantly kill an angry werewolf if I get more successes than it has Stamina?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Hyper_Intelligence_Technologies\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Hype...e_Technologies</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OK, im back to answer some questions Now with the book on my Lap.<br /> <br /> Lore of Death: IT decays the corpse of non alive creatures, in the case of mortals it will quickly kill them. occupy the same system as the one stated on the book (if you roll more sucesses than the stamina of your objective, the sucess enter as Agravated damage, if the success are lower than his stamina, they enter as bashing damage ((which i think they should enter as Lethal dammage)) This would ALSO affect the Hitmarks but in a lesser degree (like ruining their flesh skin) and it would take more time and efford. <br /> So Long story Short.<br /> Can other suppernaturals get Instakilled by this? As long they can whitstand agravated damage.<br /> Do you need to touch your target? Only if you desire. If you activate the Torment version of the power you do it to everything within the area.<br /> What happends if i roll Over the Stamina score of the target: Each success enters as agravated damage (If its a werewolf or some creature that can Resist that sort of damage, no problem)<br /> What happends if the Roll its on a creature that CANT whitstand Agravated Damage, Like a Mage or Hunter or Human even: They cant soak the agravated damage and with enough of this, they will die right away.<br /> What happends if i roll under the target's stamina points?: the damage enters as Bashing Damage to the target (I think its BS and that should enter as Lethal Damage)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Lore Of Paths, time or distace depend on a roll, must be a pre existing path. you can increace its range by doing a constant roll to add more successes to extend its path, the Faith score determines for how long this one exists. If you got a high level of torment or lesser level, humans dont see the path. they cant be affected UNLESS they walk throug that path.<br /> What happend with the obstacles: you cant pull them away, must be a clear path.<br /> How does it looks like: IF youre human with no Second Sight or any other power, the path looks like any other path, a sideway (if its activated on a street) or something similar, its pretty much invisible UNTIL you enter the Path.<br /> What if its a High Torment Version of the Power: Same as up, the path its pretty much invisible to anyone who is not INSIDE the path itself, If anyone goes INSIDE the path, go all lovecraftian/the ending of 2001 A Space Oddisey/Silent Hill/Escher/Mind breaking and insanity Inducing as you want.<br /> You mentioned Second Sight, how would that affect the look of the path?: Second sight (if youre not familiar with it) its Hunter Power that allows them to see &quot;Reality.&quot; If you have any power to see the real powers being used and effects and so on, Id magine you could see the path as a Warp Distortion/A Small BlackHole/ A Door in the middle of the Street or something similar. Be creative.<br /> Does it works like a Wormhole?: thats one way to see it. i like to explain it as the distance between to spaces becoming irrelevant, either breaking the laws of physics (by turning into an eternal path) or something incredibly short. Thing about demon powers such as those, they Warp the laws of reality so, theres not a real term to explain it. If you wanna Go with that explanation (the Wormhole) go ahead. I like to explain it as The Path being like a tense rope between Point A and B, and that the effect grabs the rope by the middle, pulling it inwards and forcing the distances between A and B to become shorter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T21:26:17-07:00","id":274470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=274091#post274091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you do go that route, you're going to need to clip some things back in order to fit the different pieces into your games. Vampire is a game that has nothing to do with spirits, so the Lupines encountered in the Antagonists section might have bizarre cults, but little to nothing about spirits is involved to keep the game in the boundaries that the V:TM core sets. Demon would likely follow the same path, especially since it never mentions spirits that aren't ghosts, I think.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, Fallen are extremely difficult to differentiate from powerful banes. In Werewolf, they would be quasi-spiritual beings that have a heavy tang of corruption about them but don't hang around the body after the Garou or Fera exorcise it, possibly in a very physical manner. Any more substantive explanation of their existence is likely to involve the old, maddened spirits of earlier geological periods that don't have much to do, like the Niobrara-spirit introduced in the W20 Book of the Wyrm. Mokole are likely to be much more familiar with them than others, other than a really old Rokea that met them but didn't care overly much about it, because you see weirder shit in a long war against the Chulorviah and merrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>P.S Demon mentions ghosts...and vampires...and in a non direct way the existance of Gaia (by being an angel of some sorts).<br /> The thing about Demons its the following.<br /> <br /> They were the first ones, no matter what. after them, the triad came over and sort of gave shape to the games. everything inside the cannon can be explained in a way related to the Triad.<br /> Vampires (wyrm)<br /> Mages (A bit of everything)<br /> Hunters (The Weaver)<br /> Changelings (No bloodey Idea)<br /> Wraiths (Wyrm..sort of)<br /> Werewolfs (Wyld)<br /> Changelings (Wyld..i think)<br /> <br /> But demons, they came before they could even be catalogued. Some claim that demons are very powerfull Banes (Like The Angel of Sorrows or The Angel of Genetic Code) While others claim that some of these beings are Gods (The Earthbound that created Rape, The Lord of Suicide, and so on) because of the creations they made...As for wraiths, i would go into heavy spoiler territory.<br /> Werewolves would easly try to kill Demons or Avoid them<br /> Nuwishas: im pretty sure that in canon, no nuwisha has ever faced one of these beings. (i play nuwisha :3 )<br /> <br /> I even belive that Icarnas could go easly by saying &quot;They are very powerful bane&quot; but not being totally sure of what they are or where do they come from since demons pretty much &quot;Popped&quot; into Existance....<br /> <br /> If anyone can show this thread to Greg Stolze or any other of the Writters from WW or Demon, i would like to get their insights about how both mythologies sort of clash.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T22:45:46-07:00","id":274510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=274470#post274470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> P.S Demon mentions ghosts...and vampires...and in a non direct way the existance of Gaia (by being an angel of some sorts).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's among the worst ways possible to mention Gaia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing about Demons its the following.<br /> <br /> They were the first ones, no matter what. after them, the triad came over and sort of gave shape to the games. everything inside the cannon can be explained in a way related to the Triad.<br /> Vampires (wyrm)<br /> Mages (A bit of everything)<br /> Hunters (The Weaver)<br /> Changelings (No bloodey Idea)<br /> Wraiths (Wyrm..sort of)<br /> Werewolfs (Wyld)<br /> Changelings (Wyld..i think)<br /> <br /> But demons, they came before they could even be catalogued. </div> </div> </div>So they claim. They're insane entities that were trapped in a place not conducive to clear thought or memory. They don't actually know, they could very well just be making a lot of shit up from the memories of their host, and since human hosts only knew what they knew as the spiritually ignorant, the so-called Elohim end up drinking their own Kool-Aid. One can only imagine what delusions Earthbound might get from hanging out in a reliquary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some claim that demons are very powerfull Banes (Like The Angel of Sorrows or The Angel of Genetic Code) While others claim that some of these beings are Gods (The Earthbound that created Rape, The Lord of Suicide, and so on) because of the creations they made...As for wraiths, i would go into heavy spoiler territory<br /> <br /> Werewolves would easly try to kill Demons or Avoid them<br /> Nuwishas: im pretty sure that in canon, no nuwisha has ever faced one of these beings. (i play nuwisha :3 )<br /> <br /> I even belive that Icarnas could go easly by saying &quot;They are very powerful bane&quot; but not being totally sure of what they are or where do they come from since demons pretty much &quot;Popped&quot; into Existance....<br /> <br /> If anyone can show this thread to Greg Stolze or any other of the Writters from WW or Demon, i would like to get their insights about how both mythologies sort of clash. </div> </div> </div>There were some details said before. Long story short, <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/archive/index.php/t-233082.html\" target=\"_blank\">you see what you want to see in the material.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-07-2014, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T04:40:19-07:00","id":274605,"title":"","content":"the gaia bit, its on the ST book so, dont blame me xD.<br /> Well, do tell me your interpretation of their existance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T05:18:25-07:00","id":274643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=274510#post274510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they claim. They're insane entities that were trapped in a place not conducive to clear thought or memory. They don't actually know, they could very well just be making a lot of shit up from the memories of their host, and since human hosts only knew what they knew as the spiritually ignorant, the so-called Elohim end up drinking their own Kool-Aid. One can only imagine what delusions Earthbound might get from hanging out in a reliquary.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use the exact same argument for the Garou: They're insane zealots who see what they want to see. The point is, you have to choose one viewpoint or the other. I know you're a diehard W:tA fan, and that's fine, but this thread seems to be focused on D:tF, so let's deal with stuff from that POV, shall we ?<br /> <br /> So yes, in D:tF, the Elohim made everytthing, the Umbras included. The Fallen seem to have only been active in making the Shadowlands, however, which was made by the seventh house for those souls who died after the Judgement. It's clear that the Fourth House also was involved as the Lore of Portals also sends you there.<br /> <br /> Gaia is most likely the angel Ziana, and her &quot;children&quot; what became of the Malhim.<br /> <br /> If that doesn't appeal to you, again, that's fine. But trying to argue that the Fallen are all too crazy to remember is just...petty and childish. And rather offensive, as you're trying to enforce your views on things onto other people, who might have tastes that differ from yours.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T08:46:27-07:00","id":274738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=274643#post274643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can use the exact same argument for the Garou:</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the exact same. The cosmological uncertainty in Werewolf is centered on where exactly Gaia and the Triat sit in relation to each other. Everything lower on the spirit hierarchy is more tangible, but also a bit more narrow in view, so you'd have to speak with an awful lot of Incarnae before you got something like a clear view from above. There's also Mnesis, which the text is hellbent on utterly discrediting with every new book. Not that Garou have access to it.<br /> <br /> But this doesn't matter, because that was my description of Demon as seen in other games. My description of Garou as seen in other games is that they aren't Garou, because of how violently we both know how they can clash with setting assumptions of Vampire, Mage and Demon. These are the &quot;minimal crossover&quot; setups, where you don't have the same werewolves as in Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're insane zealots who see what they want to see. </div> </div> </div>The &quot;see what you want to see&quot; was an out of character description of the text of Demon, specifically Days of Fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is, you have to choose one viewpoint or the other. I know you're a diehard W:tA fan, and that's fine, but this thread seems to be focused on D:tF, so let's deal with stuff from that POV, shall we ? </div> </div> </div>My argument was that you'd have to excise most of Werewolf to do this, and thus not talk about Gaia or the Umbra at all, because...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So yes, in D:tF, the Elohim made everytthing, the Umbras included. The Fallen seem to have only been active in making the Shadowlands, however, which was made by the seventh house for those souls who died after the Judgement. It's clear that the Fourth House also was involved as the Lore of Portals also sends you there. </div> </div> </div>Demon doesn't use the Penumbra that Garou go around with. What you end up with aren't Garou, but Lupines, because Demon is basically in Vampire's corner, and the only spirit world that vampires go to is the one where you see dead people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaia is most likely the angel Ziana, and her &quot;children&quot; what became of the Malhim. </div> </div> </div>There is no Gaia in Demon's setup. Don't even bother trying to port the name over. Werewolves are not known as Garou, don't call themselves Garou, and the word remains a part of the French word Loup-Garou only.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that doesn't appeal to you, again, that's fine. But trying to argue that the Fallen are all too crazy to remember is just...petty and childish. And rather offensive, as you're trying to enforce your views on things onto other people, who might have tastes that differ from yours. </div> </div> </div>Given that the games don't mix, it works out much better to just make up something than try to hammer part of a game with vastly different assumptions in. This is what we both seem to agree on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T09:47:33-07:00","id":274802,"title":"","content":"To me, Saur, this seems like thread-crapping. Some people like a unified WoD, and even if it comes at the expense at having to pick which lens they view the World of Darkness though, it's still the world of darkness. So, in short, you don't really get to tell people what to use, and what not to use, mmmkay?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T17:16:51-07:00","id":275073,"title":"","content":"Anyone else want to offer up suggestions/interpretations/house rules/whatevers of the questions I posed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T13:43:28-07:00","id":277534,"title":"","content":"For Extinguish Life I would suggest treating other supernatural beings as Demons, that is they suffer Aggravated damage if you succeed instead of instant death. In the case of the HITMark I might go as far as to say it doesn't really affect it at all, as all HIT Marks are built with the Flaw: Soulless from GttT, since they don't generally have a soul to detach from their bodies. In addition to that the HIT Marks anti-Magic defenses, ie Primium built, would likely interfere with the attack as well.<br /> Whether the ST want's to be cruel or not towards Mages in general though might affect whether or not they fall under the insta kill effect unless they have hardened their Patterns through certain rituals beforehand.<br /> <br /> As for the Lay Path. Well I would say you can create a Path anywhere your ST allows you to. Remember that you as a player define many of the details of the path, it's width, length, whether or not it reduces travel time etc and that affect your difficulty in creating the path. As for what a Path looks like you can see the description there under Find Path power, the Path created is invisible to others than it's creator barring the use of Find Path which reveals it as described therein. You want a path into a locked bank vault? Sure, just describe to your ST from where and how it twists and turns and he set's you the difficulty and you roll, should you succeed you will have a Path into it for Faith days or permanently if you use a temporary WP point, but that path is see-able to other Demons with the Lore of Paths, and likely to Mages with Correspondence. Still it is not teleporting, it is not instant and it does require physically travelling through it, as that is the domain of Lore of Portals.<br /> <br /> For the most part though I would suggest using Devil's Due rules and Demons for crossovers as they are in my humble opinion more suited for such but it is in no means impossible to crossover DtF with the other lines. Also like mentioned Demons do not really interact at all with the Umbra which may either be a problem or create a new level of intrigue and mystery to the whole chronicle as they are revealed this whole new realm of existence.<br /> <br /> Just remembered that some questions about the Lore of Paths were asked and answered in DtF Player's Guide faq section. Let's see if I can find them.<br /> <br /> Ah.. Here they are from page 15.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon Player's Guide p.15</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Can a demon (or mortal) walking a path created by the Lay Path evocation still see her surroundings?</b><br /> Yes, though the effect could be somewhat distorted and surreal depending on the nature of the path created. Lay Path manipulates spatial relationships between two points, creating paths that are entirely physical but don't necessarily correspond to three-dimensional space as the human mind perceives it.<br /> <br /> <b>If a demon makes a path through a fire, do others see him walking through the fire, or is he invisible as long as he walks on the path?</b><br /> The demon would be visible walking through the fire---a created path doesn't make a character invisible. It is possible to look for or create a path that allows character to move from point A to point B without being seen, in the same way that a person with knowledge of wilderness survival can sneak across a seemingly flat and open field by tracing a path that takes advantage of subtle dips and rises in the terrain.<br /> <br /> <b>Can a character step off a path after only walking half it's length?</b><br /> A character can exit a path at any point she wishes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So there you go hopefully all this helps you in some manner or at the least answers some of your questions.<br /> <br /> As for the use of multiple Lore's at once or combining them I'd say that is clearly Ritual area there. Though I really don't got that much good to say about the system for Rituals though, as there are even currently example rituals of direct damage effects like the Firestorm (DtPG p.191) which takes an hour to cast so that you can deal Stamina + Survival lethal damage to everyone within Faith*3 yard radius area, that is at maximum with the strongest Demon on earth casting 30 yard radius area for an hours work. You could deal a lot more damage in that time by using the free levels 1-3 Lore of Fire effects. So yeah, not really impressed with the Rituals as they are though there are some that are more reasonable like the ones used to construct Bastions.<br /> <br /> Remember though that most crossover questions cannot be answered with any certainty at all except by your own ST who is the last judge on those matters at your table.<br /> Still here are some of my opinions regarding your questions.<br /> <br /> The Umbra. <br /> Personally I'd say they didn't know about it at all, that separation happened after the War and their imprisonment. If they found out they would be surprised but perhaps pleasantly so as so far they had thought, as explained in DtF, that the world has simplifies much in their absence. Before their fall a Sword would also be a poem and a painting for example and now the discovery of the Umbrae would in their mind explain where the other possibilities went. As our world solidified into this many things were pushed into the Umbra instead of being lost. That is also how they would likely explain the spirits therein. Just another symptom of the world being cast off balance by the direct touch of the divine at the end of their Rebellion. As they have lessened in the Abyss and as they are now forced to possess material things to resist the pull of the Abyss it is perhaps only logical that they are locked away from these purely spiritual realms. Their connection to the Dark Umbra has remained strong enough for them to enter thanks to the constant pull of the Abyss and perhaps the fact they created it outside of His plans.<br /> Whether any of this is true or only how the demons explain it all to themselves is in the hands of your ST and unlikely to really come up or solve during a regular game.<br /> <br /> As for the Sense Wyrm...<br /> I'd say that Demons always ding on the Sense Wyrm scale unless were talking about Tormet 2 and under and even then I'd say that there is still a lingering Wyrm Taint there. Why so, especially when even Vampires get a free pass at Humanity 7+ (or a Road/Path that is sufficiently saintly or nature related)? Well that is because Torment is a Taint caused by their suffering in the Abyss, and some might say their actions before it, it is what separates a Demon from an Angel for the most parts, in addition to their source of Faith naturally. Torment is also scaled on Temporary and Permanent scale unlike Humanity which starts dropping like flies once you start sinning where as Torment still rises at a slow gait and can be set back by acts of Kindness. The Demons as they are just carry too much Pain, Anger, Hatred and other destructive feelings on a cosmic scale that they could be anything but strongly tied to the Wyrm. Note that this does not mean that they wouldn't on occasions bing on the Sense Gifts as well, many Demons easily ding for Sense Weaver, the Neberu especially as would likely the Annunaki, and Sense Wyld, especially the Rabisu and perhaps the Asharu, for example. Yet none of this releases them from their strong resonance with the Wyrm who is still bound as they were and just as Tormented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T20:47:58-07:00","id":279339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=277534#post277534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Demons as they are just carry too much Pain, Anger, Hatred and other destructive feelings on a cosmic scale that they could be anything but strongly tied to the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't the same be said for the garou themselves, most of whom aren't noted for being paragons of inner peace and tolerance? I wouldn't think a demon would necessarily read as Wyrm-tainted unless its motives/personality tightly corresponded to the concepts the Wyrm embodies, like corruption and decay.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T21:37:57-07:00","id":279374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=279339#post279339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Couldn't the same be said for the garou themselves, most of whom aren't noted for being paragons of inner peace and tolerance? I wouldn't think a demon would necessarily read as Wyrm-tainted unless its motives/personality tightly corresponded to the concepts the Wyrm embodies, like corruption and decay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou have a buffer of being pissed off all the time because Gaia and Luna fully intended for them to be fearsome monsters that snap at threats and pay evil unto evil in the most direct way possible. Whatever Fallen were intended to be is anyone's guess, but they aren't that anymore, and such is inherent in the fact that they are called Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T03:08:19-07:00","id":279476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=279339#post279339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Couldn't the same be said for the garou themselves, most of whom aren't noted for being paragons of inner peace and tolerance? I wouldn't think a demon would necessarily read as Wyrm-tainted unless its motives/personality tightly corresponded to the concepts the Wyrm embodies, like corruption and decay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saur Ops answered for the Garou so I'll leave that part alone for now and move on to the Fallen themselves. I'd say Torment pretty much completely falls into the concepts the Wyrm embodies like Corruption, Destruction and Decay. Note how Torment physically corrupts the Fallen twisting their Apocalyptic forms into monstrous shapes, even more corrupt and monstrous if not protected by a human buffer see Earthbound, it also corrupts and twists their Lore's into being more destructing and causing decay and corruption instead of healing for example. So all in all Torment resides pretty purely in the areas of influence that the Wyrm embodies. That is why I would make them ping for Sense Wyrm even at the low scales of Torment as the term low is somewhat relative here, their low basically meaning low enough to not actively twist them into other forms or influence their Lore's. But considering how saintly one must be for Torment 1 and 2 I might concede that the Fallen with such low amounts of Torment might actually not ping on the Sense Wyrm but I'd still keep it at might at the very least such low Torment Demons would require a higher difficulty to detect as Wyrm tainted.<br /> <br /> Again this is only my opinion as there are no definative answers for most Crossover questions and in the end it's your ST's call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T06:38:52-07:00","id":279593,"title":"","content":"Humanity 7+ Kindred don't ping for Sense Wyrm, so some Demons with low Torment could as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T08:32:42-07:00","id":279660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=279593#post279593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity 7+ Kindred don't ping for Sense Wyrm, so some Demons with low Torment could as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen unofficial rules about Torment 3 and lower not registering, I think..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T10:46:39-07:00","id":279882,"title":"","content":"Howdy.<br /> <br /> I do a load of crossover with these guys, and while I see great answers here let me just mention two house rules we use:<br /> <br /> Fallen can get into the Umbra (it almost always comes down to them being taken in by a mage since werewolves rightly won't go near 'em). Also:<br /> <span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Devils:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaver</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Defilers:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wlyd</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Devourer:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wlyd</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Fiends:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaver</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Malefactor:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaver</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Scourge:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wlyd</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Slayers:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wrym</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T17:40:10-07:00","id":281695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=279660#post279660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've seen unofficial rules about Torment 3 and lower not registering, I think..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One of the players in my game said he came across somebody's house rules that the difficulty to sense a fallen with Sense Wyrm is 10-Torment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T17:43:43-07:00","id":281725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273317-some-demon-the-fallen-questions?p=277534#post277534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Extinguish Life I would suggest treating other supernatural beings as Demons, that is they suffer Aggravated damage if you succeed instead of instant death. In the case of the HITMark I might go as far as to say it doesn't really affect it at all, as all HIT Marks are built with the Flaw: Soulless from GttT, since they don't generally have a soul to detach from their bodies. In addition to that the HIT Marks anti-Magic defenses, ie Primium built, would likely interfere with the attack as well.<br /> Whether the ST want's to be cruel or not towards Mages in general though might affect whether or not they fall under the insta kill effect unless they have hardened their Patterns through certain rituals beforehand.<br /> <br /> As for the Lay Path. Well I would say you can create a Path anywhere your ST allows you to. Remember that you as a player define many of the details of the path, it's width, length, whether or not it reduces travel time etc and that affect your difficulty in creating the path. As for what a Path looks like you can see the description there under Find Path power, the Path created is invisible to others than it's creator barring the use of Find Path which reveals it as described therein. You want a path into a locked bank vault? Sure, just describe to your ST from where and how it twists and turns and he set's you the difficulty and you roll, should you succeed you will have a Path into it for Faith days or permanently if you use a temporary WP point, but that path is see-able to other Demons with the Lore of Paths, and likely to Mages with Correspondence. Still it is not teleporting, it is not instant and it does require physically travelling through it, as that is the domain of Lore of Portals.<br /> <br /> For the most part though I would suggest using Devil's Due rules and Demons for crossovers as they are in my humble opinion more suited for such but it is in no means impossible to crossover DtF with the other lines. Also like mentioned Demons do not really interact at all with the Umbra which may either be a problem or create a new level of intrigue and mystery to the whole chronicle as they are revealed this whole new realm of existence.<br /> <br /> Just remembered that some questions about the Lore of Paths were asked and answered in DtF Player's Guide faq section. Let's see if I can find them.<br /> <br /> Ah.. Here they are from page 15.<br /> <br /> So there you go hopefully all this helps you in some manner or at the least answers some of your questions.<br /> <br /> As for the use of multiple Lore's at once or combining them I'd say that is clearly Ritual area there. Though I really don't got that much good to say about the system for Rituals though, as there are even currently example rituals of direct damage effects like the Firestorm (DtPG p.191) which takes an hour to cast so that you can deal Stamina + Survival lethal damage to everyone within Faith*3 yard radius area, that is at maximum with the strongest Demon on earth casting 30 yard radius area for an hours work. You could deal a lot more damage in that time by using the free levels 1-3 Lore of Fire effects. So yeah, not really impressed with the Rituals as they are though there are some that are more reasonable like the ones used to construct Bastions.<br /> <br /> Remember though that most crossover questions cannot be answered with any certainty at all except by your own ST who is the last judge on those matters at your table.<br /> Still here are some of my opinions regarding your questions.<br /> <br /> The Umbra.<br /> Personally I'd say they didn't know about it at all, that separation happened after the War and their imprisonment. If they found out they would be surprised but perhaps pleasantly so as so far they had thought, as explained in DtF, that the world has simplifies much in their absence. Before their fall a Sword would also be a poem and a painting for example and now the discovery of the Umbrae would in their mind explain where the other possibilities went. As our world solidified into this many things were pushed into the Umbra instead of being lost. That is also how they would likely explain the spirits therein. Just another symptom of the world being cast off balance by the direct touch of the divine at the end of their Rebellion. As they have lessened in the Abyss and as they are now forced to possess material things to resist the pull of the Abyss it is perhaps only logical that they are locked away from these purely spiritual realms. Their connection to the Dark Umbra has remained strong enough for them to enter thanks to the constant pull of the Abyss and perhaps the fact they created it outside of His plans.<br /> Whether any of this is true or only how the demons explain it all to themselves is in the hands of your ST and unlikely to really come up or solve during a regular game.<br /> <br /> As for the Sense Wyrm...<br /> I'd say that Demons always ding on the Sense Wyrm scale unless were talking about Tormet 2 and under and even then I'd say that there is still a lingering Wyrm Taint there. Why so, especially when even Vampires get a free pass at Humanity 7+ (or a Road/Path that is sufficiently saintly or nature related)? Well that is because Torment is a Taint caused by their suffering in the Abyss, and some might say their actions before it, it is what separates a Demon from an Angel for the most parts, in addition to their source of Faith naturally. Torment is also scaled on Temporary and Permanent scale unlike Humanity which starts dropping like flies once you start sinning where as Torment still rises at a slow gait and can be set back by acts of Kindness. The Demons as they are just carry too much Pain, Anger, Hatred and other destructive feelings on a cosmic scale that they could be anything but strongly tied to the Wyrm. Note that this does not mean that they wouldn't on occasions bing on the Sense Gifts as well, many Demons easily ding for Sense Weaver, the Neberu especially as would likely the Annunaki, and Sense Wyld, especially the Rabisu and perhaps the Asharu, for example. Yet none of this releases them from their strong resonance with the Wyrm who is still bound as they were and just as Tormented.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks for that. It looks like we're going with Fallen not knowing about the Umbra at first, but once they learn about it they'll be able to use Lore Of The Realms to cross over just like they can do with the Shadowlands. Still working on how they interact with the spirits there and how their Lores affect them.<br /> <br /> New question we're working on is what kinds of creatures Fallen can buff/debuff, whether or not they can do it to themselves, and what happens to buffs/debuffs of any origin when they go into their Apocalyptic Forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T13:32:07-07:00","id":284144,"title":"","content":"New questions involve a couple Lores. <br /> <br /> What's the limitation on Lore Of The Forge Level 3, Shape Object? Do I have to actually touch the object and take time, or as an evocation do I just make it into what I want? What materials can I work with? Can I use it to turn a bank vault door into a statue of a duck in moments? Can I tear through tank armor using the &quot;take matter and work it with ease&quot; part of the power? Do I have to actually make something with it, or can I use it to deform and destroy(like squeezing the barrel of a gun, putting my hand through a robot and screwing up it insides without a strength roll, etc...)?<br /> <br /> Secondly, does Lore Of Earth Level 3 sound weak? The amount of successes you roll determine the square footage you can affect, but square feet is a two dimensional amount so it's a bit weird to figure out when we're dealing with three dimensional amounts of material. How would I make spikes shoot out of the ground with it and how would I figure out how many I could make, or how high they are? Can I affect silver, steel, bronze, iron, etc... if it's part of the ground underfoot? That last might need a little clarification. In a recent session my group went against some werewolves and a mage in the party turn the ground(a sandy beach) into silver. I wanted to, in turn, turn the ground spiky to make the wolves have to take damage to get to us.<br /> <br /> Does/Can Lore Of The Spirit affect spirits in the Umbra, should the Fallen get there?<br /> <br /> Is there any way to just look into the Shadowlands without having to jump in there? Also, does the Fallen bring anything with them into the Shadowlands when they traverse using Lore Of The Realms? Can any Fallen with Lore Of The Realms move really fast, or is it Slayer specifically? The book is a little vague/confusing, saying uninitiated Fallen can't travel as fast as the Slayers but wouldn't anyone with the Lore be considered &quot;initiated&quot;? It seems to read as if the only people allowed to take or have the Lore, ever, are Slayers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}